  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Spinning Text\n\nText set on a circle that turns steadily like a rotating badge or seal.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 6 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A short slogan should circle a point like a seal, sticker or call-to-action badge.\n- An endless, steady rotation is wanted behind or around an icon or logo.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The text should read as a flat line.\n- You want text running around a tilted 3D band: use ring-text.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"learn more \\u2022 earn more \\u2022 grow more \\u2022\"\n- font_size (number, 12-160): Font size, default 56\n- radius (number, 2-14): Radius, default 5\n- color (color): Colour, default \"#171717\"\n- font_weight (enum): Font weight, default \"500\"\n- direction (enum): Direction, default \"clockwise\"\n- rotation_seconds (number, 1-30): Rotation time, default 6\n\nSource: https://github.com/magicuidesign/magicui. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Spinning Text\n\n  Text set on a circle that turns steadily like a rotating badge or seal.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/magicuidesign/magicui/blob/166367b4e31a27f166fd6c2b71d7be290fe0c1bc/apps/www/registry/magicui/spinning-text.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) Magic UI\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"spinning-text\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"6\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Text\", \"description\": \"The phrase set around the circle. A space is added at the end to close the ring.\", \"default\": \"learn more • earn more • grow more •\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Maximum text size in pixels. The ring shrinks to fit the frame.\", \"default\": 56, \"min\": 12, \"max\": 160, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"radius\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Radius\", \"description\": \"Ring radius in character widths (the source uses 5).\", \"default\": 5, \"min\": 2, \"max\": 14, \"step\": 0.5, \"unit\": \"ch\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Colour\", \"description\": \"Text colour.\", \"default\": \"#171717\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_weight\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font weight\", \"description\": \"Weight of the text.\", \"default\": \"500\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"400\", \"label\": \"Regular\"}, {\"value\": \"500\", \"label\": \"Medium\"}, {\"value\": \"600\", \"label\": \"Semibold\"}, {\"value\": \"700\", \"label\": \"Bold\"}, {\"value\": \"800\", \"label\": \"Extra bold\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"direction\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Direction\", \"description\": \"Which way the ring turns.\", \"default\": \"clockwise\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"clockwise\", \"label\": \"Clockwise\"}, {\"value\": \"counter\", \"label\": \"Counter-clockwise\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"rotation_seconds\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Rotation time\", \"description\": \"Seconds for one full turn (the source uses 10).\", \"default\": 6, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 30, \"step\": 0.5, \"unit\": \"s\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Spinning Text</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .spt-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        .spt-ring { position: relative; width: 0; height: 0; font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, system-ui, sans-serif); line-height: 1; }\n        .spt-letter { position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 50%; display: inline-block; white-space: pre; transform-origin: center; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"spinning-text\" data-duration=\"6\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"spt-clip\" class=\"spt-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"6\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"spt-ring\" class=\"spt-ring\" role=\"img\"></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/CustomEase.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function col(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, options, fallback) {\n              return options.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            // Shrink an element's font until it fits a share of the frame width.\n            function fit(el, size, share) {\n              el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var max = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * share);\n              if (el.scrollWidth > max) {\n                size = Math.max(12, size * (max / el.scrollWidth));\n                el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              }\n              return size;\n            }\n            // A seeded random generator, so every seek draws the same thing.\n            function mulberry32(a) {\n              return function () {\n                a |= 0; a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0;\n                var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a);\n                t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;\n                return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n              };\n            }\n            function clamp01(x) { return x < 0 ? 0 : x > 1 ? 1 : x; }\n            gsap.registerPlugin(CustomEase);\n            var TAG = \"spt\";\n            var bezN = 0;\n            function bez(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              return CustomEase.create(TAG + \"-\" + bezN++, \"M0,0 C\" + x1 + \",\" + y1 + \" \" + x2 + \",\" + y2 + \" 1,1\");\n            }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            function finish() {\n              var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"6\");\n              if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[\"spinning-text\"] = tl;\n            }\n\n            var ring = document.getElementById(\"spt-ring\");\n            var text = str(vars.text, \"learn more \\u2022 earn more \\u2022 grow more \\u2022\");\n            var radius = num(vars.radius, 5, 2, 14);\n            var turn = num(vars.rotation_seconds, 6, 1, 30);\n            var dir = vars.direction === \"counter\" ? -1 : 1;\n            ring.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", text);\n            ring.style.color = col(vars.color, \"#171717\");\n            ring.style.fontWeight = pick(vars.font_weight, [\"400\", \"500\", \"600\", \"700\"], \"500\");\n            var letters = Array.from(text);\n            letters.push(\" \");\n            // Fit the ring in the frame: its diameter is 2 radii (in ch) plus one letter.\n            var size = num(vars.font_size, 56, 12, 160);\n            ring.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n            var probe = document.createElement(\"span\");\n            probe.style.cssText = \"position:absolute;visibility:hidden;width:1ch\";\n            ring.appendChild(probe);\n            var chRatio = probe.getBoundingClientRect().width / size;\n            ring.removeChild(probe);\n            var room = 0.92 * Math.min(root.clientWidth, root.clientHeight);\n            size = Math.max(12, Math.min(size, room / (2 * radius * chRatio + 1.2)));\n            ring.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n            letters.forEach(function (ch, i) {\n              var s = document.createElement(\"span\");\n              s.id = \"spt-letter-\" + i;\n              s.className = \"spt-letter\";\n              s.setAttribute(\"aria-hidden\", \"true\");\n              s.textContent = ch;\n              s.style.transform = \"translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(\" + (360 / letters.length) * i + \"deg) translateY(\" + (-radius) + \"ch)\";\n              ring.appendChild(s);\n            });\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"6\");\n            tl.fromTo(ring, { rotation: 0 }, { rotation: 360 * dir * (total / turn), duration: total, ease: \"none\", immediateRender: true }, 0);\n\n            finish();\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
 "sha256": "2825ed6ad128083c288084d0c9ccebd93ebe970e34acc658f13896cd1b15fc40",
